# Daily progress tracking (Cursor)

For this project (`/common/omarmlab/members/anh/panda_project`):

## Session start (mandatory)

Before any new work on this path: run `git status` and check for modified/untracked files under `src/train/` or `scripts/`. **Commit before proceeding** — do not leave pseudo-label / Option-3 sources only on disk (2026-07-30 wipe lesson).

## Files (always keep current)

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **`DAILY_PROGRESS.md`** (project root) | **Omar-facing** day-by-day log — keep this current so Dr. Omar can open `/common/omarmlab/members/anh/panda_project/DAILY_PROGRESS.md` and see today’s work immediately |
| `outputs/DAILY_PROGRESS.md` + `outputs/docs/DAILY_PROGRESS.md` | Mirrors of the root file (same content; sync whenever root changes) |
| `outputs/EXPERIMENT_LOG.md` (+ `outputs/docs/` mirror) | Technical run log (Why→What→Result→Decision). **Never** put resume bullets or presentation copy here |

## When to update (mandatory)

After **any** of these, update **daily progress (root + mirrors) and experiment log** in the same turn (do not wait to be asked):

1. Submit, cancel, resume, or finish a Slurm train/eval/QC job
2. New best checkpoint or important metric (val or PANDA+)
3. Protocol decision (threshold, loss, skip ISUP-0, etc.)
4. Phase start/finish (Phase 1 / 2 / 3, patch extract, QC)

## How to write `DAILY_PROGRESS.md`

- Edit **`/common/omarmlab/members/anh/panda_project/DAILY_PROGRESS.md` first**, then copy to both `outputs/` mirrors
- Newest **date section at the top** (`## YYYY-MM-DD`)
- Each bullet: `- **HH:MM TZ** | What | Why | Result (numbers + job id + key path)`
- Use real local time from the cluster (`date` or log timestamps)
- Keep bullets short; link to ckpt/CSV paths, not long dumps
- Write so Omar can skim today’s section without opening other files
- Update the day’s “Open tonight / tomorrow” checklist when priorities change

## How to write `EXPERIMENT_LOG.md`

- Append/update the matching **R# / analysis** block with Why → What → Result → Decision
- Refresh **Checkpoint leaderboard** / **Active defaults** when a new teacher or protocol wins
- No resume wording, no presentation outline text

## Presentation outline

- Living slide outline: `outputs/PRESENTATION_OUTLINE.md`
- Only update when a **major phase result** changes the story (e.g. new best PANDA+ teacher, Phase 3 done)
